From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:26:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bound the shutdown gate and the wait of a disconnected
 player's removal

Lophine bounds the same waits with fixed values: 10 s for the accepted
native work a removal waits on (c99370f), and 30 s for the fake player and
Org shutdown drains (ade5106). Here each wait has one deadline, from
player-removal-timeout-seconds or shutdown-gate-timeout-seconds, so the
expiry names the stuck work and where it was registered, a stuck login's
file lease is released, and a removal the player's scheduler never runs
falls back to the region that owns the player's position. A failed region
cuts the shutdown waits to a few seconds. Lophine's drain threads, progress
logs, and the last-chance save of fake players whose removal did not finish
stay as they are; only their deadline comes from CarpetShutdownGate.

